// §14 entry 4 -- Cyrillic homoglyph across two modules -> EXS-E0105.
//
// §8.2: "Confusable detection is scoped to the IMPORT CLOSURE, not the
// compilation unit (EXS-E0105). Module A exporting Cyrillic `аdd` and
// module B calling `add` contains no confusable pair in either unit. The
// `ego` files make whole-closure checking cheap."
//
// NOT SPELLED `аdd` (spec's own illustration, Cyrillic а + Latin "dd"):
// tried that first, and tests/conformance/tools/lex_probe showed it fires
// EXS-E0104 (mixed-script identifier) all by itself, single-file, no
// closure needed -- because IT mixes Cyrillic and Latin inside one token.
// That is a true, independent diagnostic (§8.2's mixed-script rule does not
// care about modules), but it would contaminate this fixture the day
// EXS-E0105 is implemented: the same name would carry two diagnoses at
// once, and "fails with the wrong code, or an extra one" is exactly what
// CLAUDE.md says is worse than no test. Spelled instead as a
// SINGLE-SCRIPT Cyrillic homoglyph -- every letter substituted (с/c, а/a,
// р/p, е/e) -- the same shape tests/unit/lexer_ident_scripts.asm's own
// "paypal homoglyph" row uses, verified against the same probe to raise
// NEITHER E0104 nor anything else by itself.
//
// DEFERRED: needs the `ego` reader and whole-import-closure checking.
// compiler/x86_64/lexer/ident.inc's own header says this is out of a
// single-file lexer's reach BY CONSTRUCTION ("NOT HERE: EXS-E0105 ... A
// single-file lexer cannot see a closure ... it lands with the `ego`
// reader") -- not a gap in this wave's lexer, the next stage's job
// entirely, and nothing under compiler/x86_64/lexer/ is expected to change
// for it.
//
// Represented as two "modules" in one file, clearly marked, because there
// is no multi-module driver yet for two real files to be "the same
// fixture" through -- once one exists, this should become two files.

// ---- "module A": exports a name that LOOKS LIKE Latin "cape" -----------
// Every letter below is its Cyrillic look-alike -- с (U+0441), а (U+0430),
// р (U+0440), е (U+0435) -- so the identifier is single-script Cyrillic,
// not mixed-script: it is confusable with Latin "cape", not internally
// mixed the way `аdd` was.
publica functio саре(x: mensura, y: mensura) -> mensura {
    redde x + y
}

// ---- "module B": imports and calls the Latin-spelled name --------------
publica functio combina(x: mensura, y: mensura) -> mensura {
    redde cape(x, y)   // Latin `cape` -- no such name exists in THIS file,
                        // but is confusable with module A's export once
                        // both are in one import closure: EXS-E0105
}

// TEST: entry=4 shape=code expect-code=EXS-E0105 status=deferred needs=import_closure
